  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADVANCING CLIMATE ADAPTATION AT SCALE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Climate Resilience of vunerable developing countries by:Fiscal Resilience Facility &#x2013; provides technical assistance to Finance Ministries to make finance flows consistent with a pathway towards low greenhouse gas emissions and climate-resilient development. Support will focus on the Pacific Region. Adaptation Strategy for Atolls &#x2013; funding will support analytic work in one of the four Atoll countries (Kiribati, Maldives, the Republic of the Marshall Islands (RMI), and Tuvalu) including the development of adaptation pathways; Climate Adaptation Investment Planning &#x2013; support will focus on one country in the Pacific and one in Southeast Asia, helping to develop an adaptation investment plan for one specific sector; and Community Resilience Partnership Program &#x2013; support will strengthen capacity at local level, especially of local governments and grassroots women&#x2019;s organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
